}{\plain \fs24 \b\f1 Reception of the Body}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The following form may be used at whatever time the body is brought to\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 the church}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 .}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The Celebrant meets the body at the door of the church and says}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3402\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3402\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \f1 With faith in Jesus Christ, we receive the body of our brother\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 (sister) }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 N}{\plain \fs24 \f1 . for burial. Let us pray with confidence to God, the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Giver of life, that he will raise }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 him}{\plain \fs24 \f1  to perfection in the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 company of the saints.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Silence may be kept; after which the Celebrant says}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Deliver your servant, }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 N}{\plain \fs24 \f1 ., O Sovereign Lord Christ, from all\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 evil, and set }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 him}{\plain \fs24 \f1  free from every bond; that }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 he}{\plain \fs24 \f1  may rest with\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 all your saints in the eternal habitations; where with the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Father and the Holy Spirit you live and reign, one God, for\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 ever and ever.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 Amen}{\plain \fs24 \f1 .\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Let us also pray for all who mourn, that they may cast their\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 care on God, and know the consolation of his love.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Silence may be kept; after which the Celebrant says}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Almighty God, look with pity upon the sorrows of your\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 servants for whom we pray. Remember them, Lord, in mercy; \softline
nourish them with patience; comfort them with a sense of your \softline
goodness; lift up your countenance upon them; and give them \softline
peace through Jesus Christ our Lord. }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 Amen}{\plain \fs24 \f1 .\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 If the Burial service is not to follow immediately, the body is then\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 brought into the church, during which time a suitable psalm or anthem\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 may be sung or said. Appropriate devotions, such as those appointed for\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 the Vigil on page 465, may follow.}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20  \par
